        "text": "The 2026 Black Duck report found 93% of commercial codebases carry zombie components — dependencies with no development activity in two years. A January preprint argues AI-assisted development is accelerating the crisis by breaking the engagement loops that sustain maintainers. Meanwhile, one open-source project fixed three user-filed bugs in nine hours flat — and has had daily commits for over two hundred consecutive days, partly through an autonomous AI agent handling maintenance.",
